{
  "date": "2026-11-05",
  "id": "1385",
  "title": "Find the Distance Value Between Two Arrays",
  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/find-the-distance-value-between-two-arrays/",
  "topics": [
    "Array",
    "Two Pointers",
    "Binary Search",
    "Sorting"
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Given two integer arrays arr1 and arr2, and the integer d, return the distance value between the two arrays."
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "The distance value is defined as the number of elements arr1[i] such that there is not any element arr2[j] where |arr1[i]-arr2[j]| <= d."
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Example 1:"
    },
    {
      "t": "code",
      "v": "Input: arr1 = [4,5,8], arr2 = [10,9,1,8], d = 2\nOutput: 2\nExplanation: \nFor arr1[0]=4 we have: \n|4-10|=6 > d=2 \n|4-9|=5 > d=2 \n|4-1|=3 > d=2 \n|4-8|=4 > d=2 \nFor arr1[1]=5 we have: \n|5-10|=5 > d=2 \n|5-9|=4 > d=2 \n|5-1|=4 > d=2 \n|5-8|=3 > d=2\nFor arr1[2]=8 we have:\n|8-10|=2 <= d=2\n|8-9|=1 <= d=2\n|8-1|=7 > d=2\n|8-8|=0 <= d=2"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Example 2:"
    },
    {
      "t": "code",
      "v": "Input: arr1 = [1,4,2,3], arr2 = [-4,-3,6,10,20,30], d = 3\nOutput: 2"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Example 3:"
    },
    {
      "t": "code",
      "v": "Input: arr1 = [2,1,100,3], arr2 = [-5,-2,10,-3,7], d = 6\nOutput: 1"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Constraints:"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "• 1 <= arr1.length, arr2.length <= 500"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "• -1000 <= arr1[i], arr2[j] <= 1000"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "• 0 <= d <= 100"
    }
  ]
}
